          "question": "1. **Group Invariance (UMPI)**: Let $X_1, \\dots, X_m \\overset{\\text{iid}}{\\sim} \\mathcal{N}(\\mu_1, \\sigma_1^2)$ and $Y_1, \\dots, Y_n \\overset{\\text{iid}}{\\sim} \\mathcal{N}(\\mu_2, \\sigma_2^2)$ be two independent normal samples where all four parameters $(\\mu_1, \\mu_2, \\sigma_1^2, \\sigma_2^2)$ are unknown. Consider testing $H_0 : \\sigma_1^2 \\le \\sigma_2^2$ against $H_1 : \\sigma_1^2 > \\sigma_2^2$ at level $\\alpha$. Identify the natural location-scale transformation group $\\mathcal{G}$ that leaves this testing problem invariant, find the maximal invariant $M$ acting on the sufficient statistics $(\\bar{X}, \\bar{Y}, S_X^2, S_Y^2)$, and derive the Uniformly Most Powerful Invariant (UMPI) test.\n2. **Pitman Asymptotic Relative Efficiency (ARE)**: Let $Z_1, \\dots, Z_n$ be an i.i.d. sample from a location family $f(z - \\theta)$ where $f(u)$ is symmetric about $0$ with variance $\\sigma^2 < \\infty$ and positive density $f(0) > 0$ at the median. Derive the Pitman Efficacy of the one-sample Sign Test $S_n = \\frac{1}{n} \\sum_{i=1}^n \\mathbf{1}_{\\{Z_i > 0\\}}$ and the Student's $t$-test for testing $H_0 : \\theta = 0$ versus $H_1 : \\theta > 0$, prove the general formula $\\text{ARE}(S, t) = 4 \\sigma^2 [f(0)]^2$, and evaluate $\\text{ARE}(S, t)$ under both the **Normal** distribution and the **Laplace (Double Exponential)** distribution.",
