          "question": "Suppose observations follow the location model $X_i = \\theta + \\varepsilon_i$, where the error $\\varepsilon_i$ follows a Student-$t$ distribution with $\\nu > 2$ degrees of freedom and density:\n\n$$f_\\nu(x) = \\frac{\\Gamma\\left(\\frac{\\nu + 1}{2}\\right)}{\\sqrt{\\nu \\pi} \\, \\Gamma\\left(\\frac{\\nu}{2}\\right)} \\left( 1 + \\frac{x^2}{\\nu} \\right)^{-\\frac{\\nu + 1}{2}}, \\quad -\\infty < x < \\infty$$\n\n1. Using the known variance $\\sigma_\\nu^2 = \\text{Var}(\\varepsilon_i) = \\frac{\\nu}{\\nu - 2}$ (for $\\nu > 2$) and evaluating the quadratic density integral $\\int_{-\\infty}^\\infty f_\\nu^2(x) \\, dx$, derive the closed-form formulas for $\\text{ARE}(\\text{Sign}, t; t_\\nu)$ and $\\text{ARE}(\\text{Wilcoxon}, t; t_\\nu)$ as functions of $\\nu$.\n2. Evaluate $\\text{ARE}(\\text{Sign}, t; t_\\nu)$ and $\\text{ARE}(\\text{Wilcoxon}, t; t_\\nu)$ numerically for $\\nu = 3$, $\\nu = 5$, and in the Gaussian limit $\\nu \\to \\infty$.\n3. Explain the physical and statistical behavior of both AREs as $\\nu \\to 2^+$ (where variance diverges) and at $\\nu = 1$ (the Cauchy distribution).",
